%% HTTP prefix: /api/v1. API lane includes verified middleware and errorHandler.
%% Grouped read and validation calls short-circuit on error. No Repository layer is implied.
%% Issue and notification helpers use the global Prisma client inside the locking wrapper, not its tx client. Do not infer atomic rollback.
sequenceDiagram
    actor A as Receptionist
    participant UI as API client
    participant API as Express middleware / errorHandler
    participant C as attendance.controller.ts
    participant S as receptionAttendanceService
    participant DB as Prisma / PostgreSQL

    A->>UI: Submit violation report with explanation
    UI->>API: POST /api/v1/attendance/reports
    activate API
    API->>API: authenticate, checkFacilityScope, authorizeExact(RECEPTIONIST)
    alt request guard rejects
        API-->>UI: 400 / 401 / 403 error
    else request accepted
        API->>C: submitViolationReport(req, res, next)
        activate C
        C->>S: submitAttendanceViolationReport(user, input)
        activate S
        S->>DB: Begin transaction, lock pair, recalculate attendance and read existing unresolved report
        activate DB
        DB-->>S: Requested records and validation context
        deactivate DB
        S->>S: Require absence at least 30 percent and no existing OPEN / IN_PROGRESS / RESOLVED report
        alt threshold not met, duplicate open or approved report, or inaccessible pair
            S->>DB: Roll back transaction
            S-->>C: 400 / 404 / 409
        else business conditions satisfied
            S->>DB: Create Issue containing verified attendance report metadata and notify facility Manager
            activate DB
            DB-->>S: Saved result
            deactivate DB
            S->>DB: Commit transaction
            S-->>C: Submitted attendance report without immediate removal
        end
        deactivate S
        C-->>API: response or next(error)
        deactivate C
        API-->>UI: 201 report or mapped error
    end
    deactivate API
    UI-->>A: Show result or actionable error
%% UI_SCOPE: Backend/API implemented. Current application UI route is not verified as reachable.
